  "summary": "Curved bamboo penjor poles and woven palm-leaf offerings dressing Bali in daily devotion.",
  "description": "Balinese ritual craft turns the island into an installation: Galungan's penjor — tall bamboo poles bent at the tip like dragon tails, hung with woven coconut-leaf garments, rice cakes and fruit — line every road, while women place canang sari, palm-leaf square trays of flowers, betel and rice, before shops and shrines each dawn. Lamak banners, gebogan fruit towers and temple gate hangings follow the same intricate palm-leaf weaving grammar (jejaitan). The craft encodes tri angga cosmology: sky, air and earth in every arrangement.",
